/target

# Dev-only local override: `[patch.crates-io]` pointing at a sibling checkout outside this
# repository (the `pmpx-plugin` contract crate). Cargo fails hard on a patch aimed at a missing
# path, so committing this would break every lone clone and every CI run.
/.cargo/config.toml

# `plugin-asset` writes the two release assets here when it is run locally; CI uploads
# them straight from the runner, so nothing in here is ever committed.
/dist

# Cargo.lock is committed on purpose, unlike a plain library. CI resolves with
# `--locked`, so the lockfile is what records which contract crate the mapping was
# checked against.
